---
// A reply editor: typing "/regr" opens the picker, then a formatted response lands.
const items = [
  { key: '/regression-slope', desc: 'SLOPE cell points to wrong range' },
  { key: '/regression-chart', desc: 'Trendline missing equation' },
  { key: '/regression-great', desc: 'Everything checks out' },
];
---

<div class="axiom relative aspect-[16/10] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-[#080a10]" data-inview aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="absolute bottom-0 right-0 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-accent/15 blur-3xl"></div>

  <div class="absolute inset-[6%] overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line-strong bg-[#0d1017] shadow-2xl shadow-black/60">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-4 py-2.5">
      <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-faint">Reply to Jordan · Topic 1 DQ 2</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-accent">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent"></span> Axiom
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="relative p-4">
      <p class="typed font-mono text-[12px] text-fg"><span class="typed-text"></span><span class="caret">▍</span></p>

      <div class="picker absolute left-4 right-4 top-11 rounded-lg border border-line-strong bg-raised p-1.5 shadow-xl shadow-black/50 sm:right-auto sm:w-[70%]">
        {items.map((it, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-md px-2.5 py-1.5 ${i === 0 ? 'item-active' : ''}`}>
            <span class="font-mono text-[10.5px] text-fg">{it.key}</span>
            <span class="hidden truncate text-[10px] text-faint sm:inline">{it.desc}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="inserted space-y-2 text-[11.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p class="text-fg">Hi Jordan,</p>
        <p>
          Nice work on the scatter plot. In cell <span class="rounded bg-accent-soft px-1 font-mono text-accent">B18</span>, your
          <span class="font-mono text-fg">=SLOPE()</span> uses the x-values as y. Swap the ranges and you should get
          <span class="font-mono text-signal">2.47</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="absolute bottom-3 right-4 font-mono text-[10px] text-faint">inserted in <span class="text-signal">0.4s</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .typed-text::after {
    content: '';
  }
  .in .typed-text::after {
    content: '/regr';
    animation: type 1.2s steps(1) forwards;
  }
  .caret {
    animation: blink 1s steps(1) infinite;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .picker {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px) scale(0.98);
  }
  .in .picker {
    animation: picker 2.4s 1.1s var(--ease-out-expo) forwards;
  }
  .item-active {
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }
  .inserted {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
  }
  .in .inserted {
    animation: insert 0.8s 3.3s var(--ease-out-expo) forwards;
  }
  .in .typed {
    animation: hide 0.01s 3.3s forwards;
  }
  @keyframes type {
    0% { content: '/'; }
    25% { content: '/r'; }
    50% { content: '/re'; }
    75% { content: '/reg'; }
    100% { content: '/regr'; }
  }
  @keyframes blink {
    50% { opacity: 0; }
  }
  @keyframes picker {
    0% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px) scale(0.98); }
    15%, 85% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    100% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-4px); }
  }
  @keyframes insert {
    to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }
  @keyframes hide {
    to { opacity: 0; height: 0; }
  }
</style>
